---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
	title="Beyond VaR"
	category="Survival Analysis · Quantitative Finance"
	year="2026"
	summary="A quantitative risk framework that extends Value at Risk from the magnitude of losses to the duration of post-loss recovery."
>

	<div class="project-block">

		<div class="project-label">
			Overview
		</div>

		<div class="project-main">

			<h2>
				Risk is not only how much you lose.
			</h2>

			<p>
				Beyond VaR studies both the magnitude of abnormal
				ETF losses and how long it takes an asset to recover
				after those losses occur.
			</p>

			<p>
				The project combines conventional Value at Risk
				methodology with survival analysis to provide a
				duration-based perspective on financial risk.
			</p>

			<div class="project-tags">

				<span>Survival Analysis</span>
				<span>Value at Risk</span>
				<span>Quantitative Finance</span>
				<span>Python</span>
				<span>ETFs</span>
				<span>Risk Modeling</span>

			</div>

		</div>

	</div>


	<div class="project-block">

		<div class="project-label">
			Methodology
		</div>

		<div class="project-main">

			<h2>
				From loss events to recovery duration.
			</h2>

			<p>
				The framework analyzes daily returns for SPY, QQQ,
				GLD and VOO and identifies abnormal downside events
				using rolling one-day VaR estimates.
			</p>

			<ul>
				<li>
					Historical Value at Risk
				</li>

				<li>
					Parametric Normal Value at Risk
				</li>

				<li>
					Monte Carlo Value at Risk
				</li>

				<li>
					Kupiec and Christoffersen VaR backtesting
				</li>

				<li>
					VIX as a market-stress covariate
				</li>

				<li>
					Event-level data preparation for survival analysis
				</li>
			</ul>

		</div>

	</div>


	<div class="project-block">

		<div class="project-label">
			Interface
		</div>

		<div class="project-main">

			<h2>
				Analysis designed to be explored.
			</h2>

			<p>
				The project also includes an interactive Streamlit
				dashboard for exploring VaR estimates, violations,
				backtesting results and market-stress conditions.
			</p>

			<p>
				A separate Power BI dashboard provides an executive
				view of ETF VaR breaches, severity and risk indicators.
			</p>

		</div>

	</div>


	<div class="project-block">

		<div class="project-label">
			Project
		</div>

		<div class="project-main">

			<h2>
				The Dawn of WLs.
			</h2>

			<p>
				Beyond VaR is a collaborative project developed as
				part of The Dawn of WLs.
			</p>

			<div class="project-links">

				<a
					href="https://github.com/the-dawn-of-WLs/Beyond-VaR-Modeling-Post-Loss-Recovery-Duration-with-Survival-Analysis"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>
					View GitHub ↗
				</a>

			</div>

		</div>

	</div>

</ProjectLayout>
